+Rate merging follows AmpliCol's trial-count weighting, including the variance
+from differences between iteration means. Production errors use its population
+second-moment convention. These are native Monte Carlo estimates under adaptive,
+nonzero-count stopping, not an independent fixed-size estimator or a claim of
+exact finite-sample unbiasedness.
+
+Each production iteration completes a requested number of **nonzero folded
+observations**. The initial pilot requests the generated event quota or 1,024 nonzero
+points, whichever is larger. Further requests double and account for the
+remaining event demand using observed acceptance and the tail checks. This
+pilot replaces AmpliCol's preproduction warmup schedule: MG5 has already
+performed a separate survey. Iterations complete their nonzero request rather
+than stopping early on a provisional candidate count. Zero points
+contribute to integration statistics but do not fill this nonzero quota. Trial
+and iteration limits are failure guards, not successful completion criteria.
